## 3. Sample Queries and CRUD Operation Results

The queries below were executed against a live MySQL/MariaDB instance running `database_setup.sql`. Output is the actual terminal result, not illustrative.

### CREATE — Insert a new transaction

```sql
INSERT INTO Transactions (category_id, financial_transaction_id, amount, fee,
    balance_after, currency, transaction_datetime, sms_date_received, status, raw_body)
VALUES (2, 'FTX10006', 15000.00, 150.00, 53850.00, 'RWF',
    '2024-05-16 10:00:00', '2024-05-16 10:00:02', 'completed',
    'Payment of 15000 RWF to merchant completed');
```

**Result:**

| transaction_id | category_id | financial_transaction_id | amount | fee | status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 7 | 2 | FTX10006 | 15000.00 | 150.00 | completed |

*(Insert screenshot of this query and result here)*

### READ — Join a transaction with sender, receiver, and category

```sql
SELECT t.transaction_id, tc.category_name, t.amount, t.currency,
    su.full_name AS sender, ru.full_name AS receiver, t.transaction_datetime
FROM Transactions t
JOIN Transaction_Categories tc ON t.category_id = tc.category_id
JOIN Transaction_Participants sp ON t.transaction_id = sp.transaction_id AND sp.role = 'sender'
JOIN Users su ON sp.user_id = su.user_id
JOIN Transaction_Participants rp ON t.transaction_id = rp.transaction_id AND rp.role = 'receiver'
JOIN Users ru ON rp.user_id = ru.user_id
WHERE t.transaction_id = 1;
```

**Result:**

| transaction_id | category_name | amount | sender | receiver | transaction_datetime |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Incoming Money | 20000.00 | Jane Smith | Alex Doe | 2024-05-10 14:32:00 |

